      "writtenOn": "2021-02-11T22:56:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t have any context into the storage issue here, so I cannot speak to that. But regarding the user code:\n\nWhen does this storage code get exercised? Does this mean that cleanupPreCreatedUsers() can now be called even not during boot-up? Is that safe? I believe this method is currently only called at boot, and perhaps relies on that assumption.\nIn particular, what if someone is trying to upgrade a pre-created user into a full user at the same time? Might we wind up *slating* the pre-create for removal, then upgrading it, and only then removing it (thereby destroying a regular user!)?\n\nAny thoughts Felipe?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5065,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 5065,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "601b49c4f2207847e06ef3dd0dbb2132bbbf656f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9870ddb9_2d8c0197",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/UserManagerService.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 5065,
      "author": {
        "id": 1013984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-16T16:38:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, I meant to reply earlier, but forgot to finish the comment.\n\nI think removing the pre-created users when the storage is moved is fine, it\u0027s safer than try to \"salvage\" the pre-created users data.\n\nThe pre-created users are not necessarily pre-created at boot, they could be at any time (in fact, we\u0027re changing the workflow on Automotive to created them when the device is shut down / goes into garage mode).\n\nAnyways, the goal of pre-creation is to optimize the (real) creation time, but correctness is more important, so cleaning up these users when it would be hard to fix / change their state is a good compromise to me.",
      "parentUuid": "a8bbf820_eab16276",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5065,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 5065,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "601b49c4f2207847e06ef3dd0dbb2132bbbf656f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "204fdd33_e1790a86",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/UserManagerService.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 5065,
      "author": {
        "id": 1165283
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-17T19:06:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When I said \"at boot\", I mean that cleanupPreCreatedUsers() is currently called at boot, not that the precreated user is created at boot.\n\nI\u0027m concerned that if we can also call cleanupPreCreatedUsers() later-than-boot then we need to address potential race conditions that could result in removing fully created users (or in-the-process-of-becoming fully created users).\n\nE.g., what would happen if this method were invoked in the middle of a separate thread running\nconvertPreCreatedUserIfPossible()?\nI think we could end up deciding to upgrade a precreate, but then making that precreate \u0027removed\u0027 before we actually finish the upgrade, resulting in a garbage user.\n\nWe need to think about that carefully and either convince ourselves we\u0027re safe or lock to avoid the races, etc..",
      "parentUuid": "9870ddb9_2d8c0197",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5065,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 5065,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "601b49c4f2207847e06ef3dd0dbb2132bbbf656f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
